> >I got polymorhed to a baby crocodile by a ring (which I then
> >removed) and am now unable to move and I'm getting hungry. If
> >I die of starvation while polymorphed do I return to my
> >original form, preferably in a non-starving state?

> Dying while polymorphed will turn you back, but I'm not sure
> how this affects the hunger state of your old body.

> You can move by dropping some stuff. Crocodile-you can't wear
> armor anyway.  Don't go TOO far away, so nothing can pick up
> your stuff, and you can get back when you revert, but don't
> just sit overburdened (and therefore getting hungrier faster)
> in one place hoping for the best.

When I'm polymorphed into something I don't want to be, I'll
usually drop everything but a couple of daggers, and then throw
them up in the air.  Seems to be about the fastest way of
returning to normal.  (Of course, if there are monsters around,
you don't need to bother.  They'll take care of returning you to
normal quicker than you might want.)

